# =============================================================================
# GODOT 4
# =============================================================================

# the editor's own cache: imported textures, shader cache, editor layout.
# regenerated on open, and machine-specific — never commit it.
.godot/

.nomedia

# FIXED: this line used to read `.import/	export.cfg` — two patterns
# separated by a tab. git reads a line as ONE pattern, so it was matching a
# path literally called ".import/<tab>export.cfg" and neither entry did
# anything. Split apart below.
#
# NOTE the trailing slash on `.import/`: that restricts the match to a
# DIRECTORY of that name (a Godot 3 leftover). It must never become
# `*.import`, which would exclude the per-asset .import files Godot 4
# generates — those are required metadata and DO belong in the repo.
.import/

export.cfg
export_credentials.cfg
*.tmp


# =============================================================================
# MONO / C#
# =============================================================================

.mono/

# CAREFUL: this is `data_*` with an underscore, so it does NOT match this
# project's own data/ folder (items, pets). Do not "tidy" it to `data*/` —
# that would silently stop tracking every item definition in the game.
data_*/

mono_crash.*.json


# =============================================================================
# BUILD OUTPUT AND SCRATCH  (added)
# =============================================================================

# exported builds — large, regenerable, and they change on every export.
builds/

# working files from Claude sessions: debug renders, sprite-sheet contact
# strips, notes. Useful while working, not part of the game. Godot generates
# .import files for any image left in the project folder, which is why these
# were showing up as assets.
Claude outputs/

# a stray near-duplicate of project.godot. The hyphen matters — this pattern
# does NOT match project.godot itself.
project-*.godot

# the test suite's transcript, rewritten on every run. The suite writes it
# because neither the editor's Output panel nor a Windows terminal could be
# relied on to show its results — see src/tools/testrunner.gd.
test_results.txt


# =============================================================================
# HISTORY-REWRITE SCRATCH
# =============================================================================

# Working files from the git-filter-repo pass that moved the art pack out of
# this repo's history: path inventories, object-id dumps, before/after diffs.
# About 2MB of them, and they are what the rewrite CONSUMED, not what it
# produced - the rewritten history is the output and it is already in .git.
#
# LISTED INDIVIDUALLY rather than as *.txt, because a blanket rule would also
# swallow a real notes file someone adds later and nobody would notice until
# it was missing.
#
# Checked before ignoring: none of them name a .db, a .env, a password or a
# token - they are art paths and SHAs. Ignoring here does NOT untrack them;
# see the note in README/DEVLOG for the `git rm --cached` that does.
current-all.txt
current-all2.txt
current-art.txt
historical-paths.txt
historical-paths-raw.txt
objects.txt
pack-files.txt
packshas.txt
purge-paths.txt
remaining-raw.txt


# =============================================================================
# OS CRUFT
# =============================================================================

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Written by Settings.set_graphics_api() beside project.godot. It is one
# machine's choice of renderer, which is the definition of a file that must
# not follow the project to another machine.
override.cfg

# Commit message drafts used with git commit -F. Scratch, not record.
commit_*.txt
